  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Weequery 3.1.0.\n\nBEHAVIOUR. BindingResolutionSettings.Default now leaves out anything marked [NotMapped], so BindResolve and\nResolveBindables with no settings no longer bind a property the model says is not a column. A caller filtering\nin memory on one loses it; assign IgnoreAttributes = [] to keep the 3.0 behaviour.\n\nAdded: BindingResolutionSettings.IgnoreAttributes. A property carrying a listed attribute is not bound, nor is\nanything below it, nor a property whose type carries one, nor a quantifier over a collection whose element type\ndoes. Assigning a set replaces the default one, so spread Default.IgnoreAttributes in to add to it. An entry\nthat is not an attribute type is refused.\n\nFaster: BindResolve keeps what it binds, collections included, for the process, under the depth, the settings\nand the use it was asked for. A repeated call walks nothing and builds nothing, and costs about what binding a\ncached request set does. Settings are compared by what they hold, so settings built fresh for every request still\nfind the entry.\n\nThe companion packages are released alongside at the same version.",
